{"title":"Topicwise Test-1 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EC Network -1","fileName":"052_Topicwise Test-1 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EC Network -1.html","branch":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electronics Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown in the figure, the value of current <img src=\"/media/8301d5e7f81a40ccd5c1b8becf933e61898a16d9.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/2c52d7080232448e5ae9200654dc0eb7445dbfce.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1.43 A</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1.48 A</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1.37 A</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 1.67 A</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/1edaeea6d244ddabab4e118c5fb71989005ec1b6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The capacitors (C) are arranged as shown in figure below, to obtain a capacitance value of 4 μF rated for 900 V.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/308d52ed475e9cf9e0a07e6dc00d04bd22fe7faf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The maximum charge stored by a capacitor is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 3.6 mC</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1.2 mC</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 2.2 mC</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 2.4 mC</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/b7b3a7569e6c65439a9d02a93ed2167b88da4632.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below, choose which of the following KCL equations is correct for node <em>A</em>?</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9e1ede485696fef5b10a36e8bfebdce50b3bd8c1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/523a646a4a0e99a9ebcd9c4a385a8fe39914ae75.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/91ca9bcecd337fef2776c0bf7479ce722b1a2f46.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/47e3a5dea938af7f1a4e1fe58c021253241e2c0e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/6ef4287e07296c90a092e97608e3fe259d24466b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/b5418db5bf03e2ee1b5a22944fc55b515b5f4f33.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>In the interconnection of ideal sources shown in the figure, it is known that the 90 V source is absorbing power.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/f3771c5e0cc80b75de91f896bb2e13dacefab384.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Which of the following can be the value of current source <img src=\"/media/ca078ad173c77d9c8161921e3b6986fd0864dc2a.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> and resistance ‘R’?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 12 A; 15.625 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 18 A; 10 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 12 A; 10 Ω</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 21 A; 15.625 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/4eebe8813a23cd8807a1393fe12449726adbbc2d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/c8ec45448792e28d44b560b4ba23ecad886db2a3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below, what should be the value of resistance ‘<em>R<sub>s</sub></em>’ so that load <em>R<sub>L</sub></em> = 2 kΩ will get maximum power?</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/229b1abcf0011502b9ac523b61e286cf554f6501.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 4 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 8 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nTo get maximum power to load resistance (<em>R<sub>L</sub></em>), &lsquo;<em>R<sub>s</sub></em>&rsquo; should be as minimum as possible. Hence, option (d) is most suitable answer.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/0b093e57a5948debeb0a06def57e93967d0835c9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The Thevenin’s equivalent resistance seen across the terminal <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> is ________ Ω.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"10.4","high":"10.4"},"solution":"<p>10.4 (10.1 - 10.7)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/e13ac5c38c11d93c29c0dc9a4651d2662678609f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In a series RLC circuit, <em>L</em> = 40 mH is given. If the instantaneous voltage and current are 50 cos <img src=\"/media/cfcf9179806f8807cec5337ed734a39bc92f6fd4.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> and 20 cos(628<em>t</em> – 25°) A respectively, the quality factor of the circuit is ________. (correct to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"10.29","high":"10.29"},"solution":"<p>10.29 (10.00 - 11.05)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/65ecd87a338da95ff65650be3ae642c14a01a9ec.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/7775f137a2948e9d989331aecdfe317e6f57837e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown in the figure below, the Norton’s current across the load <em>R<sub>L</sub></em> is 10 A. Then, the value of <em>R</em> is ________ Ω.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/2552a882d416056f22dd9544e8e5c4944703f4ac.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.6","high":"0.6"},"solution":"<p>0.6 (0.6 - 0.6)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/29650ad01de05a216ff579522a2b3ea2ab7e0263.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/44137b44f87e111ddf3f8391503259f8be9ccf59.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Which of the following option(s) is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> The current through 10 Ω resistance is 7 A.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>The Norton’s current (Short circuit current) <img src=\"/media/5d7999a5f1686f05aad5f4399d82e90cdd30074f.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> across 10 Ω is 14.92 A.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>The open circuit voltage (<em>V</em><sub><em>O</em>.<em>C</em></sub>) across 10 Ω is approx. 85 V.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>The Thevenin’s equivalent impedance (Z<sub>th</sub>) across 20 Ω is approx. 5.72 Ω.</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b, c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/ea33343bec87102cdd43eed4fd72c906e42303b0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/84a227d8738d5f2168969eaf7d349dc0c02c50f3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/c6e47aaaa0695e6b05fd94c9d582390b79d32e77.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/4d46851cf4c64b70fed9c9d890e4ad88fdb008a4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The equivalent capacitance seen across the terminal <em>a</em> and <em>b</em> is _______ F.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 7 F</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 3.34 F</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 2.34 F</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 6 F</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9aa9c44a20185088930c03d78e822d7ff728eccd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/39e547bd9a46130f12b9ca24735f8d39fd304cf0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/718109adc3765dd112edf9f6f6e24381a6584374.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>What should be the value of resistor ‘<em>R</em>’ such that the energy stored in the circuit is 512 J?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 25 Ω</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 50 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 8.33 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 12.33 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/92ee5779cf34310a376043852368c30832864f26.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d150997783261edbc0ed7a4715bc8f44d5d853b9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Two currents are represented by <img src=\"/media/84ef06ca1f9024f2c874e5ab3e581d77f88236ba.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> These currents are fed into a common conductor. If the conductor has a resistance of 5 Ω, the energy loss in 24 hours will be</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 91.4 × 10<sup>6</sup> J</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 9.14 mJ</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 914 Joule</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 9.14 × 10<sup>8</sup> J</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/e4407996084fa18f17cdb3cca7b535da2f237890.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A resistor <em>R</em> in series with a capacitance <em>C</em> is connected to a 240 V-50 Hz ac apply. The value of <em>C </em>so that <em>R</em> absorbs 150 W at 50 V is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 80 μF</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/2245f024fb9e559f735d34fa8b6bbc2d94f3b798.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 40.68 μF</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/8246503844d9eb248acc22f4922e25aac898a499.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/340f0e083ec3e8b2f97dfce228f37deb4dcd8297.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The phase difference between <img src=\"/media/50bdfbd8be68f0e9bfad74ffaa3aebefbe29afe0.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> and <em>V</em><sub>2</sub> is _______ degree. (correct to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"65.05","high":"65.05"},"solution":"<p>65.05 (64.00 - 65.80)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9ce4efc7da14af9b43ddb8cfb7eec0363c095542.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d52b30ca32e843c3558a5f01d7352858adbe33cf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The current <img src=\"/media/cac3f70482929ce79a3c52380bc61125cbfc3637.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> through 5 V voltage source is _________ A. (correct to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4.28","high":"4.28"},"solution":"<p>4.28 (4.25 - 4.29)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/73baf4126fe4f03ea0943cc04de3c1c6b7c4fc0e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d85f9820bf98b168e4315c481757bfbef3a0676b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In the series circuit shown in figure, for given V-I values, the value of the coupling coefficient K will be ________. (correct to two decimal places)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/863fb830d147422816e4063a7e2af4c7d7196531.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.43","high":"0.43"},"solution":"<p>0.43 (0.42 - 0.44)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/357cec201235dbf2681e16de9449f59d2d0c0460.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A RLC circuit having resistance <em>R</em> = 10 Ω, inductance <em>L</em> = 2 mH and capacitance <em>C</em> is connected such that:<br />\n<strong>Condition I:</strong> For getting quick oscillation free output for an ac input in series connect RLC circuit.<br />\n<strong>Condition II:</strong> We get quality factor (Q) equal to 3 if the above elements are connected in parallel.<br />\nConsidering the above information, select the correct option(s).</p>\n<p> </p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> For condition-I to satisfy; <em>C</em> must be 80 μF.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> For condition-I to satisfy; <em>C</em> must be 0.05 F.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> For condition-II to satisfy; <em>C</em> must be 0.18 mF.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Both the conditions can’t be satisfied at a time for any value of <em>C</em>.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, c, d)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/6817d565ce5c0a3b2c8e984ab65dc0cd4fc014a0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:15.610Z"}